The Following is a list of ToolTypes for this ICON:


NOTICE: ALL TOOLTYPES ARE CASE SENSITIVE

ABOUT: This ICON may be any name you wish it to be. You should find some
       pre-defined SERIAL.DEFS in the STORAGE/SERIAL directory.

       This defines how your serial.device should be configured per unit.

       This ICON must be in the NODE/SERIAL directory for any node which is
       tied to a modem.


SERIAL.UNIT=
SERIAL.BAUD=
SERIAL.DRIVER=
SERIAL.A2232_PATCH


SERIAL.UNIT=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells which UNIT of the serial.device to use for a particular /X
          NODE.

     SERIAL.UNIT=2


SERIAL.BAUD=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells /X which Baud to initialize the serial port to.

     SERIAL.BAUD=19200


SERIAL.DRIVER=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells /X which serial driver to use for a particular /X NODE.

     SERIAL.DRIVER=serial.device


SERIAL.A2232_PATCH

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells /X to patch the internal /X serial routines to allow certain
          version of the 2232 card to be compatible with /X.

     SERIAL.A2232_PATCH


